      "content": "wait, glucose-lowering snacks? u mean like fruit? but i thought carbs make blood sugar go up... if i'm already feeling dizzy and shaky from the spike, wont eating fruit make the spike way worse? i'm confused. i just want to know if the extra insulin is the right move to get back to normal quickly so i can just pass out and sleep.",
